{title: 389 - Light of Light, Enlighten Me}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Doctrines}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Gm]Light of light, enlighten me,
[Bb7]Now anew the day [Fm]is dawning;
[Bb/F]Sun [Cm/G]of [Bb7/Ab]grace, the [Cm/G]shadows [Gm/Bb]flee;
[Gb]Brighten Thou [Gbm]my [Gm]Sabbath [Bb]morning;
[Bb/D]With Thy joyous [Am]sunshine blest,
[Bb]Happy is my day of rest.

Verse 2:
[Gm]Let me with my heart today,
[Bb7]Holy, holy, holy, [Fm]singing,
[Bb/F]Rapt [Cm/G]awhile from [Gm]earth away,
[Gb]All my soul [Gbm]to [Gm]Thee up [Bb]springing,
[Bb/D]Have a foretaste [Am]inward given
[Bb]How they worship Thee in heaven.

Verse 3:
[Gm]Hence all care, all vanity!
[Bb7]For the day to God [Fm]is holy;
[Bb/F]Come, [Cm/G]Thou [Bb7/Ab]glorious [Cm/G]Majesty,
[Gb]Deign to fill [Gbm]this [Gm]temple [Bb]lowly;
[Bb/D]Nought today [Am]my soul shall move,
[Bb]Simply resting in Thy love.
